course: dictionary
lesson: 7214
title: What is philosophy?
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Philosophy is the study of big questions about life, knowledge, right and wrong, the mind and what is real. You answer these questions by thinking carefully and giving reasons, not just by guessing.
explain: The word comes from Greek and means «love of wisdom». «Philosophy is careful thinking about big questions.» So a philosopher is someone who enjoys thinking hard about questions like these.
explain: The word can also mean a set of ideas, or your own way of living. «My philosophy is to always try my best» tells you what a person believes about how to live. Look at the words around philosophy to decide which meaning is being used.
fact: Philosophy means careful thinking about big questions about life, knowledge, right and wrong, the mind and what is real.
fact: The word philosophy comes from the Greek for "love of wisdom".
fact: «Philosophy» can also mean a particular set of ideas, like the philosophy of Plato.
fact: A person's philosophy is their way of thinking about how to live or work.
fact: Some schools do "philosophy for children", where pupils discuss questions and give reasons for their answers.
exercise: «Philosophy comes from the Greek for "love of wisdom".» What does the word philosophy mean? | Study of animals | Fear of hard questions | Love of sport | *Love of wisdom
exercise: In «philosophy for children», pupils discuss questions like «Is it ever OK to lie?» What do they do? | Copy notes from the board | Only watch videos | Run races outdoors | *Discuss the question and give reasons
exercise: Mia says, «My philosophy is to always try my best.» What is her philosophy? | A school subject about maths | *Her way of thinking about how to live | A type of plant | The name of her teacher
test: In «Idealism is the philosophy that reality is made of minds and ideas», what does philosophy mean? | A type of weather | A kind of food | A school break | *A particular set of ideas
test: Which of these is a philosophy question? | How many legs does a spider have? | What is 7 times 8? | *Is it ever right to break a promise? | Which colour is the sky?
exam: Which of these best describes philosophy? | Drawing pictures of animals | Memorising dates from history | *Careful thinking about big questions, giving reasons | Running fast to win a race
